  "manual": {
    "message_age": "scapy's age is a BCDFloatField in seconds while the wire carries 16-bit 1/256 s units (i2m = 256x), so int sentinels overflow the 2-byte pack and the per-bit probe cannot run; offset 27 follows IEEE 802.1D-2004 Fig. 9-1 and the [build, expected] crosscheck pair verifies the bytes",
    "max_age": "scapy's maxage is a BCDFloatField in seconds while the wire carries 16-bit 1/256 s units (i2m = 256x), so int sentinels overflow the 2-byte pack and the per-bit probe cannot run; offset 29 follows IEEE 802.1D-2004 Fig. 9-1 and the [build, expected] crosscheck pair verifies the bytes",
    "hello_time": "scapy's hellotime is a BCDFloatField in seconds while the wire carries 16-bit 1/256 s units (i2m = 256x), so int sentinels overflow the 2-byte pack and the per-bit probe cannot run; offset 31 follows IEEE 802.1D-2004 Fig. 9-1 and the [build, expected] crosscheck pair verifies the bytes",
    "forward_delay": "scapy's fwddelay is a BCDFloatField in seconds while the wire carries 16-bit 1/256 s units (i2m = 256x), so int sentinels overflow the 2-byte pack and the per-bit probe cannot run; offset 33 follows IEEE 802.1D-2004 Fig. 9-1 and the [build, expected] crosscheck pair verifies the bytes",
    "root_mac": "6-byte MAC fields take no integer probe sentinel (scapy builds MACs from strings); the wire bytes are crosscheck-verified",
    "bridge_mac": "6-byte MAC fields take no integer probe sentinel (scapy builds MACs from strings); the wire bytes are crosscheck-verified"
